    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on maximizing efficiency against softer arms, anchored by two elite starts: **Vinnie Pasquantino** (69.03) and **Trevor Story** (69.17). **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a highly favorable matchup against Law, where his massive 14% platoon boost elevates him to our top-tier target for 1B production. Meanwhile, **Trevor Story** capitalizes on a high-value combination of a hitter-friendly park and a generous xERA matchup, making him a cornerstone of the middle infield today. While **Seiya Suzuki** (64.25) and **Brice Turang** (60.78) sit just inside the strong start threshold, they are essential for our primary goal of mitigating SB scarcity, as both players benefit from tactical advantages against their respective opposing batteries that allow them to aggressively challenge for bags despite the presence of elite holding pitchers.\n\nThe most difficult lineup decision today involved the marginal quadrant of our roster, specifically the choice to start **Zach McKinstry** (40.62) while keeping a tight leash on **Austin Riley** (41.42). While **Austin Riley** technically holds a higher raw projection, his matchup against Luzardo is marred by a severe 19% SP skill penalty and a lower batting order slot that caps his ceiling. **Zach McKinstry** ultimately stays in the lineup due to park factors, though we are monitoring the pending status of **Edwin Arroyo** (40.91); should **Edwin Arroyo** be relegated further down the order or benched entirely, he will be pulled immediately to protect our game caps. **Max Muncy** (45.06) remains a high-variance play today\u2014we are knowingly sacrificing efficiency against the elite arm of Dylan Cease, but his park-adjusted power profile provides enough potential for a cheap HR to keep him rostered for now. With **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Mickey Moniak** all unavailable today, our depth is thin, placing the burden of production squarely on the shoulders of **James Wood** (48.76) to leverage his elite xwOBA despite facing a tough assignment in Pivetta.",
